    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Embraced in 412 A.D. as a Roman patrician's prot\u00e9g\u00e9, Gracis Nostinus survived the murder of his beloved sire Marius by their barbarian blood-brother Hrothulf &mdash; a betrayal Gracis has never stopped avenging in spirit, blaming Rome's entire fall on the loss of men like Marius. Fleeing to the New World over the centuries, Gracis has built one of the largest personal followings in Milwaukee's @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.fc464242d84d4e34]{Camarilla} and now openly campaigns to become the city's next Prince following the previous Prince's death, believing only strong central rule can save Milwaukee from the factional war threatening to draw Justicar attention. He speaks six languages fluently and cultivates an image as an effete, fussy intellectual, but commands genuine political weight through eight Retainers and extensive Influence, Resources, and Allies.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Prim, effeminate, and fastidious &mdash; wipes his hands after any physical contact, speaks through his nose, hunches to seem shorter than his five feet. Underneath the foppish affect is a serious, patient political operator obsessed with restoring order.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Marius (slain by Hrothulf, Marius's own childe, in a sudden frenzy circa 412 A.D.). Rival: Hrothulf. Haven: a luxurious waterfront home north of Downtown. Disciplines as printed: Auspex 3, Dominate 4, Fortitude 3, Presence 4 (capped above to this system's 1-5 scale).",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
